Sliding window with a set of characters currently in the window. Move `right` forward, add each character; if it's already in the set, shrink from `left` until it's gone. Track the max window size. O(n) time, O(min(n, alphabet)) space.

```js
function longestUniqueRun(s) {
  const seen = new Set();
  let left = 0, best = 0;
  for (let right = 0; right < s.length; right++) {
    while (seen.has(s[right])) {
      seen.delete(s[left]);
      left++;
    }
    seen.add(s[right]);
    best = Math.max(best, right - left + 1);
  }
  return best;
}
```

Empty string returns 0 since the loop never runs.

Sliding window with a set of characters currently in the window. Move the right pointer forward, and when the incoming character is already in the set, advance the left pointer and delete characters until it's gone. Track the max window size.

```js
function longestUniqueRun(s) {
  const seen = new Set();
  let left = 0, best = 0;
  for (let right = 0; right < s.length; right++) {
    while (seen.has(s[right])) {
      seen.delete(s[left++]);
    }
    seen.add(s[right]);
    best = Math.max(best, right - left + 1);
  }
  return best;
}
```

O(n) time, O(min(n, alphabet)) space. Empty string returns 0 naturally.
